From 5c5dc2e4f4b46e3b71abe675fff672474569fad3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Askham <harryaskham@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 23:38:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bd-fbdd22: lock-free cached nudge-wake agent lookup (registry
 read-contention)

handle_agent_nudge -> state.agents.get takes the contended AgentManager inner
lock; under sustained registry-write load it blanks/times-out (bd-4e5f59 bounds
it but the lookup still fails) -> the nudge returns a backpressured envelope
instead of resolving the local agent. Registry-side sibling to bd-057f2e.

Fix: AgentManager::get_cached, a lock-free lookup from the existing
agents_read_model (the lock-free read-model landed under bd-dc4a4c, refreshed
off the hot path by the reconcile loop). handle_agent_nudge tries get_cached
first (no inner lock; common established-agent case) and falls back to the
bounded lock-based get only on a cache miss (cold model, agent newer than the
~10s refresh, or a Discarded agent). The duplicate-spawn-guard
find_any_agent_for_bead callers intentionally stay lock-based (need a fresh
view to avoid missing a recent worker -> duplicate spawn).

+ unit test get_cached_resolves_from_read_model_bd_fbdd22.
